{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSaQa6mm9en9vdSaudp7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — No status field currently on Order model\n- OrderController.kt:15-46 — Only supports create, get, and list operations\n- OrderRepository.kt:10-27 — In-memory store, no method to query by orderId for related entities\n- Shipment.kt:9-14 — Already has ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController.kt:15-56 — Create, get, list operations; no validation on order state\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27 — No method to find shipments by orderId\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum centralized; no ORDER_CANCELLED code yet\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-28 — Catches ApiException and builds standardized error envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409)\n2. Error responses wrapped in ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n3. In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap with standard CRUD methods\n4. Models are Kotlin data classes\n5. Tests use SpringBootTest + MockMvc and validate error envelope shape, not just status\n6. Enums for state like ShipmentStatus\n\n**Affected files and why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. **Order.kt** — Must add `status` field and define `OrderStatus` enum\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Must add POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full logic\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Must add method to find all shipments for an order (to validate/cancel them)\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must check order status when creating shipment, reject if CANCELLED\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code for shipment creation rejection\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests for all cancel cases per ticket\n\n**Risks:**\n1. **Idempotency**: Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order must succeed silently, not fail\n2. **Atomicity**: If any shipment is CONFIRMED, the entire operation must roll back — order stays ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged\n3. **State consistency**: Shipment creation must be rejected if order is CANCELLED, but only for this order (other orders unaffected)\n4. **Existing test fragility**: Adding status field to Order requires updating existing create response to include it\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — the ticket clearly specifies all behavior and error cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field; add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Newly created orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Retrieves order by ID; throws 404 if not found\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, returns 200 with the order (idempotency)\n   - If order is ACTIVE, check all its shipments: if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) with ORDER_CANCELLED code without modifying anything\n   - If ACTIVE and no CONFIRMED shipments exist, set order to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save all, return the updated order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Before saving a shipment, check if the order exists; if it does, also check if order status is CANCELLED, and if so throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum (used when creating shipment for cancelled order).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add comprehensive tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order returns 200 unchanged (idempotency)\n   - Cancelling with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and leaves everything unchanged\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Existing tests must still pass (they won't check status field if not asserted)\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n- **Alternative 1**: Store cancellation state as a separate flag (e.g., `isCancelled: Boolean`) instead of an enum. Rejected because the ticket says \"An order gains a status\" and the shipment model already uses an enum; consistency is better, and it leaves room for future statuses.\n\n- **Alternative 2**: Handle shipment cancellation in a separate service layer. Rejected because the codebase has no service layer yet; repositories are injected directly into controllers, which is the existing pattern. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring out of scope.\n\n- **Alternative 3**: Add a separate error code for each rejection reason (e.g., SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER vs ORDER_CANCELLED). Rejected because a single code is sufficient; the message distinguishes the case. Adding unnecessary codes clutters the API contract.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Validation | Write | Status | Body |\n|------|-------|------|-----------|-------|--------|------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE, no CONFIRMED shipments | orderId | Order, Shipments for that order | Order exists, no CONFIRMED | Order→CANCELLED, Shipments→CANCELLED | 200 | Order with status=CANCELLED |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED | orderId | Order | Order exists | None | 200 | Order unchanged, status=CANCELLED |\n| Cancel ACTIVE with CONFIRMED shipment | orderId | Order, Shipments | Order exists, has CONFIRMED | None | 409 | Error: ORDER_CANCELLED, order/shipments untouched |\n| Cancel non-existent order | orderId | Order lookup fails | - | None | 404 | Error: ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | request | Order, Shipment lookup | Order is CANCELLED | None | 409 | Error: ORDER_CANCELLED |\n| Create shipment for non-existent order | request | Order lookup fails | - | Shipment saved | 201 | Shipment (unchanged behavior) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **test_cancel_active_order_succeeds** — Create ACTIVE order, call cancel, assert 200, order is CANCELLED\n2. **test_cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments** — Create ACTIVE order, add CREATED shipment, cancel, assert shipment is now CANCELLED\n3. **test_cancel_active_order_preserves_confirmed_shipments_on_conflict** — Create ACTIVE order, add CONFIRMED shipment, call cancel, assert 409, order still ACTIVE, shipment still CONFIRMED\n4. **test_cancel_idempotent** — Create order, cancel it, cancel it again, assert 200 and unchanged\n5. **test_cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404** — Call cancel on non-existent ID, assert 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n6. **test_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_rejected** — Create and cancel order, try to create shipment, assert 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n7. **Existing tests must pass** — Ensure order creation and retrieval still work (they won't check status but won't break either, given that it defaults to ACTIVE)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":20299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1047},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"232a9e75-3184-455d-8cb0-25298b2f31f3","uuid":"64e4619c-a2c8-438d-a54d-6c2ebac07b72","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:08:41.376Z","request_id":"req_011CfSaQZjCf3CkL2LLRpqTx"}
